# Every path rule here is anchored with a leading slash so it matches only at
# the repo root. Unanchored, `.claude/commands/` would also match
# plugins/cairn/.claude/commands/ and silently untrack every plugin's shipped
# slash commands — the same trap that hid temper's own command file for months
# (a bare `TEMPER.md` pattern matched .claude/commands/temper.md at depth).

# Review output and local install state.
#
# The suite's own tools write to .aether/out/: /critique-plan writes CRITIQUE.md,
# /critique-diff appends TEMPER.md, and enforce-whetstone.sh drops a .nudged
# sentinel. Per-developer, per-session scratch that means nothing in someone
# else's checkout. .aether/config and .aether/rules.md are NOT ignored — those
# are project settings worth committing.
#
# .aether/plans/ is the same kind of scratch in the same directory: plan files
# are per-developer working state (Claude Code plan mode has its own ignored
# equivalent in /.claude/plans/), not project settings.
/.aether/out/
/.aether/plans/
/.aether/manifest
/.aether/hooks/

# Plan files themselves stay in plan mode's own directory.
/.claude/plans/

# Artifacts of a local install.
#
# This repo is the installer, so `bash install.sh` without --global writes its
# output straight into the working tree: the suite hook and its gates, copies of
# every plugin's slash commands, the CLI, and the manifest. All are generated
# from files that are already versioned under plugins/.
#
# /.claude/settings.json is deliberately absent: a project may want to share it.
/.claude/hooks/
/.claude/commands/
/.claude/aether.manifest
/.bin/

# The same for the other agents: .agents/skills/ is what scripts/build-skills.sh
# generates from plugins/ — exactly what .claude/commands/ is for the engine —
# so it is never committed. scripts/install-skills.sh rebuilds it on every
# install rather than copying a possibly-stale checkout.
/.agents/

# Backups written before install.sh and uninstall.sh mutate settings.json or
# CLAUDE.md in place.
*.bak

# macOS
.DS_Store
